## IBM Z HMC API Implementation

The metrics and entities defined in the `mainframe` and `virtualization` namespaces are
sourced from the IBM Z Hardware Management Console (HMC) Web Services API. Each metric
and attribute definition in `model/mainframe/` carries an `annotations.hmc_source` block
that records the exact HMC metric group or object property, operating mode, and minimum
HMC version.

Two hand-authored documents provide the implementation reference:

- **[HMC API Signal Mapping](../hmc-api-signal-mapping.md)** — Full cross-reference
  table mapping every OTel metric to the HMC metric group, field name, required
  transformation, and key discriminating attributes. Organized by domain (environmental,
  processor, memory, I/O, network, crypto, partition).

- **[HMC API Background](../hmc-api-background.md)** — Architecture overview, entity
  construction tables (how each OTel entity attribute maps to an HMC API object and field),
  unit conversion reference, collector pipeline configuration, and platform-specific caveats
  (Classic vs DPM mode, processor type cardinality, NNPA availability, metrics context
  lifecycle).

> **Note:** When the upstream Weaver template package adds support for rendering
> `annotations.hmc_source` blocks, the signal mapping will be generated directly from
> the model YAML annotations and these hand-authored files will be retired.
